                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Caveman Warriors is a game that was abandoned not only by players who had played for a couple of hours, but even by the developers themselves. I bought the game because it reminded me of The Flintstones on SEGA. But I was wrong. I completed the game 100%, but I can’t say I enjoyed it, because it’s a terrible, buggy, nasty, and clunky game. At first, I played with a friend, but when we reached the fifth level, he flatly refused to keep playing, explaining that the game was just a piece of junk. But I didn’t give up, and I completed the game on normal difficulty and on arcade mode. I got 54 achievements out of 55, but I still didn’t get the last achievement — “Caveman Warrior”. Because even the achievements in this game are buggy. (You can check the topic in the discussions.) I strongly advise against buying this game, as well as other games by JanduSoft.\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\n⠀⠀⣰⣷⣄⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⣰⣿⣷\n⠀⠀⣿⣿⣿⡄⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢠⣿⣿⣿⣆\n⠀⢠⣿⣿⣿⣿⣄⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⣾⣿⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⣸⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣴⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⡇\n⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⠛⠉⠛⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⠋⠉⠻⣿⡿\n⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⠇⢀⣶⡄⢸⣿⣿⣿⠀⢰⣶⡀⢻⡿\n⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿⣿⠈⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿⣇⠀⣿⣷\n⢰⣿⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿⣿⠀⣿⣿\n⢸⣿⣿⣿⣿⣄⣿⣿⣿⣼⣿⣿⣧⣀⣿⣿⣿⣼⣿⣿\n⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⡿⣻⣿⣿\n⠀⠹⣿⣿⣿⣆⡏⢟⠿⡿⠿⠿⢿⡛⠹⡄⣠⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⠀⠻⣿⣿⣿⣿⣼⠊⢣⠎⠱⡎⣘⣧⣾⣿⣿⡿⠁\n⠀⠀⠀⠘⢿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⡿⠛⠁\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢀⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⠉⠉\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⣾⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣧\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⣰⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⡄\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⠀⣀⠾⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⡿⠧⣀\n⣠⣡⣀⠀⢦⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⠀⡐⡙\n⢿⠀⠁⠰⢰⣿⣿⣿⡿⠿⢿⣿⣿⣿⡸⠉⠈⠇\n⠈⠓⢤⣤⢾⣿⣿⣿⡇⠀⠀⣿⣿⣿⣧⠴⠋\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⢸⣿⣿⣿⠃⠀⠀⣿⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⠈⣿⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀⠈⣿⣿⣿\n⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠈⠉⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠉⠉",
